# The performer of the verb phrase it stands in: in an instruction, the controller of the spell or
# ability unless a Handoff names another; in a clause, what its active Subject or its `by` agent
# names. An `action` Definition's body reads its call's performer through `$actor` instead, which
# does not rebind inside the body. Prints no word; `subject` reads what the verb phrase is said of
# as a participant.
primitive actor: NounPhrase = Actor
